From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] t41: build the recovered ISP driver on Linux 7.x

Port the recovered T41 driver and its V4L2 frontend from the vendor 4.4
API to the mainline 7.x API:

- add a T41 kernel-compat header and object for the removed 4.4 helpers
- use copy_from_kernel_nofault, i2c_new_client_device, kernel_read/write,
  kmalloc, timer_setup/timer_delete_sync, ioremap/iounmap
- read platform_data through the struct, not the 4.4 +0x5c offset
- replace the raw 4.4 struct resource arrays with real resource structs
- translate the vendor IRQ numbers (hwirq + 8) to Linux virqs through the
  T41 core-intc domain
- adapt the V4L2 frontend to the 7.x videobuf2 API and VFL_TYPE_VIDEO;
  skip registration when the parent device has no driver bound
- add bring-up diagnostics around the subdev IRQ and memory setup

Load-tested on the T120; the probe path is being brought up.
---
